(6067340, 891774, 73942, '<td valign="top">I agree with <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=99263" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">ThingFish</a>, I loved this shot and actually gave it a 10.  Should of ended  higher.</td>', 'I agree with  ThingFish, I loved this shot and actually gave it a 10.  Should of ended  higher.', '2010-06-23 08:18:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(6067344, 891667, 69008, '<td valign="top">It makes an interesting line that the first four masts are the same height.  Overall it''s a very pleasing shot. The Moon and Venus are a nice touch, and on the whole, the shot is very similar to something that I would shoot.  <br/>This was probably shot RAW, with WB processed from there. I shoot JPG, using tungsten/incandescent WB, for night shooting, and it takes the street light orange out of the sky, giving it a sweet blue cast.</td>', 'It makes an interesting line that the first four masts are the same height.  Overall it''s a very pleasing shot. The Moon and Venus are a nice touch, and on the whole, the shot is very similar to something that I would shoot.  This was probably shot RAW, with WB processed from there. I shoot JPG, using tungsten/incandescent WB, for night shooting, and it takes the street light orange out of the sky, giving it a sweet blue cast.', '2010-06-23 08:33:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(6067349, 890922, 69008, '<td valign="top">I also see the white balance being off a little, but I can''t tell exactly what it needs to correct it.  It could be that your monitor needs calibration, and you can''t see it at your computer. Try looking at the photo on someone else''s computer.   <br/>This would look good in B&amp;W too.  I agree about the composition being very pleasing.</td>', 'I also see the white balance being off a little, but I can''t tell exactly what it needs to correct it.  It could be that your monitor needs calibration, and you can''t see it at your computer. Try looking at the photo on someone else''s computer.   This would look good in B&W too.  I agree about the composition being very pleasing.', '2010-06-23 08:41:50.000000', NULL, 0),
